  "generated_text": "1. Identify the years after 1994 on the graph: 1996, 1998, 2000, and 2002.\n2. Determine the sales amounts for these years:\n   - 1996: 2.4 million dollars\n   - 1998: 3 million dollars\n   - 2000: 4.2 million dollars\n   - 2002: 5.2 million dollars\n3. Calculate the increase in sales for each year:\n   - 1996 to 1998: \\(3 - 2.4 = 0.6\\) million dollars\n   - 1998 to 2000: \\(4.2 - 3 = 1.2\\) million dollars\n   - 2000 to 2002: \\(5.2 - 4.2 = 1.0\\) million dollars\n4. The largest increase is from 1998 to 2000 with an increase of 1.2 million dollars.\n\n\\(\\boxed{2000}\\)",
